// A `void *` takes an array of an element type an array crosses as, or a `ByteBlock`, and nothing
// else: not an array of strings, not a scalar, not an array whose length no parameter carries (the
// second pointer `memcmp` reads, whose length is the first's), and C writes no value through one
// marked `out`: it fills an array or a struct mirror through one.
// error: parameter 2 of the C binding `writeStrings` is `Array[string]` in Avin and `const void *` in C: an array crosses to C as `Array[byte]`, `Array[int]`, `Array[long]`, `Array[real]` or an `Array` of a struct mirror, whose elements C reads
// error: parameter 2 of the C binding `compare` is `Array[byte]` in Avin and `const void *` in C: C could read past the end of an array whose length nothing carries: mark the integer parameter that carries it `length(b)`
// error: parameter 2 of the C binding `writeScalar` is `long` in Avin and `const void *` in C: `const void *` points at memory of no type, so it takes an `Array[byte]`, `Array[int]`, `Array[long]` or `Array[real]`, its length in bytes carried by the parameter marked `length(buf)`, or a `ByteBlock`
// error: the result of the C binding `find` is `long` in Avin and `void *` in C: C answers a pointer to memory of no type, whose length nothing says, so a `void *` result crosses as nothing: a binding whose result is `unit` discards it
// error: out value 1 of the C binding `sysctlOut`, `oldp`, is `int` in Avin and `void` in C: C writes no value through `out void *oldp`, which points at memory of no type: pass an array or a `ByteBlock` for C to write, as in `void *oldp, length(oldp) size_t n`, or answer what C fills, an array named with `array: "oldp"` and its length in bytes given with `length:`, or a struct mirror

@c("ssize_t write(int fd, const void *buf, length(buf) size_t nbyte)")
writeStrings(fd: int, buf: Array[string]) -> long

@c("int memcmp(const void *a, const void *b, length(a) size_t n)")
compare(a: Array[byte], b: Array[byte]) -> int

@c("ssize_t write(int fd, const void *buf, size_t nbyte)")
writeScalar(fd: int, buf: long, n: long) -> long

@c("void *memchr(const void *s, int c, length(s) size_t n)")
find(s: Array[byte], c: int) -> long

@c("int sysctlbyname(const char *name, out void *oldp, inout size_t *oldlenp, null void *newp, size_t newlen)")
sysctlOut(name: string, oldlen: long, newlen: long) -> (int, int, long)

main()
  println(0)
